\subsection*{Index of identifiers and pages}
\phantomsection
\addcontentsline{toc}{subsection}{Index of the 324 routes: identifier and page}
\label{sec:vi-indice-rutas}

Each identifier links to the beginning of its record. The indicated page
is the printed page number of the volume. Identifiers are read by rows,
from left to right, preserving the order of the unified table.
The PDF bookmarks panel also allows the reader to select the cell first
and then the horizontal and vertical orientation. The four orientations
of a cell are distinct routes, not versions of a single record.

